# Agent working agreement: repo-root AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md are tracked POINTERS
# to the canonical /aux/koutecky/logseq/tine-agents/AGENTS.md (kept outside the
# worktree so `git clean` can't delete it). They are tracked on purpose — a
# tracked file survives `git clean`; do NOT ignore them.

# Local agent scratch — subagent task specs + notes, and the internal
# deferred-work list. Working artifacts between Martin and Claude, not shared.
/subagent-tasks
/DEFERRED.md

# Private Reddit outreach data — keep locally, never publish
reddit-backup/

# Lane evidence (receipts, gate baselines, necessity/fail-before logs). Workers
# write these to the worktree root; the manager archives them under
# tine-agents/evidence/ before integration. They must never be tracked: they
# leak private worktree paths and dossier names to both public remotes
# (census guard g_h_repository_root_tracks_no_lane_evidence).
/RECEIPT*.md
/baseline-*.txt
/necessity-*.txt
# Every root-level log, not an enumeration of the shapes lanes have used so far:
# the list below had grown to nine patterns and still missed *-pass-after.log,
# *-debug.log and *-gate.log, which is most of what a lane actually writes. No
# root .log file has ever been tracked, so the wide rule costs nothing and a lane
# can no longer invent a name that escapes it.
/*.log
/*-cargo-metadata.json
/after-*.txt
/measurement-*.txt
/measurement*-*.md
# A sandboxed lane cannot write the default npm cache directory, so it makes one
# here. It is a build artifact, not source.
/.npm-cache/
